# GPU plugin: size the paged-attention intermediate buffers from the current call, not the last one
#
# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0001-0015. Applied to the staging build used for the byte-identity ladder below and for
# the unit tests; not applied to production and not to any packaged level. CHANGELOG.md and
# contrib/packaging/marfrit-openvino updates are deferred to the next release, same as
# patches/0015.
#
# Status: a correct hardening of a real stale count. The deep-prompt crash this patch was once
# tested against is diagnosed elsewhere (DESIGN.md 7.0.2ad) as a driver/runtime fault outside
# this plugin - a page-fault storm at a fixed GPU virtual address that the OpenCL runtime's own
# allocation log identifies as its direct-submission semaphore buffer, evicted under VRAM
# pressure and never re-validated before the next wait - and this patch neither causes nor closes
# it.
#
# This patch's own evidence is the unit tests below (two red-first review tests, the asymmetric
# deep-pool regression and the repeated-execute growth regression) and the byte-identity ladder
# at 8,418 tokens (u8:i4, chunk 128, unbounded, a 16 GiB card). Both measured on a clean build of
# the shipped stack (the pinned baseline + patches 0001-0016, nothing else): all 19 tests in the
# combined filter pass on the 24 GB card, and 0015+0016 is 6 of 6 runs byte-equal to the
# untouched plugin's output (the untouched plugin itself shows about one outlier run in
# fourteen, the stack's own run-to-run noise, which this patch does not add to). An earlier
# staging build that also carried an unrelated experimental change was 5 of 6 on the same
# ladder and 18 of 19 on the tests, the one failure being the sliding-window test's own fixture
# (an unsized cache), since repaired.
#
# Harness fact, for the record: a single paged-attention primitive, one network, executed
# repeatedly like a served prefill (u8:i4, MIXED chunks of 128 or 256 tokens, past 0 up to
# 100,352 tokens, PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS 0 or 32) passes 4/4 in the unit-test harness -
# and this IS the repeated-execute case (m_rt_params non-null after the first call, intermediates
# reallocating on the growth chunks, exactly the branch this investigation is about), unlike every
# single-shot test elsewhere in this file (one network, one execute() call, m_rt_params always
# null on that first and only call). It does not, and structurally could not, exercise the fault
# diagnosed above: that fault needs real VRAM pressure and concurrent host/device load a small,
# isolated unit-test dispatch does not create.
#
# get_internal_buffer_descs() (paged_attention_opt.cpp) sizes internal buffers exp_sums,
# max_logits, tmp_out - the ones the SDPA_STAGE_0 kernel writes per-partition softmax state into
# and the finalization kernel (SDPA_STAGE_1) reduces (named by role, not number: the descs are
# packed densely and has_scores_output() shifts every index from exp_sums onward by two, so
# there is no single fixed number for any of these - in the no-scores MIXED-stage indexing
# arcint serves it is exp_sums=3, max_logits=4, tmp_out=5, and index 6 is the gws->subsequence
# mapping; the construction sites size each correctly regardless of which index it lands at,
# which is why this patch's own read and fix are unaffected by getting the number wrong) - once
# per call, from whichever of two sources looked available:
#
#   if (rt_params != nullptr && rt_params->num_of_partitions != 0) {
#       num_of_partitions = rt_params->num_of_partitions;      // "already computed, reuse it"
#   } else {
#       ... num_of_partitions = ceil_div(max_context_len, partition_size);  // compute fresh
#   }
#
# Read (not measured) call order, from primitive_inst.cpp: primitive_inst::execute() calls
# realloc_if_needed() -> realloc_intermediates(), which calls get_internal_buffer_descs() to
# decide whether exp_sums/max_logits/tmp_out need to grow, BEFORE _impl->execute() runs - and it is
# _impl->execute() that calls update_rt_params(), the only place that assigns
# rt_params->num_of_partitions for the call about to be dispatched. m_rt_params is a member the
# implementation keeps across calls; update_rt_params() overwrites its fields in place and
# nothing resets num_of_partitions to 0 between calls. So on every call after the first, the
# "already computed" branch above is taken - but what it reuses is the PREVIOUS call's
# num_of_partitions, not the one the kernels about to run will use. exp_sums/max_logits/tmp_out
# sizing is structurally one call behind the dispatch that writes into them.
#
# realloc_intermediates()'s own reuse logic (buffer kept if the new request's byte count fits
# within _max_intermediates_memory_sizes[i], the historical high-water mark) means this does not
# corrupt every call - once some earlier call's FRESH sizing (the else branch, run before any
# rt_params exists, or a call where rt_params was for some other reason zero) has pushed a
# buffer to a given size, later calls whose stale reuse asks for less than that keep the larger
# buffer untouched. The gap only opens on the specific call that reaches a partition count no
# earlier call's fresh sizing ever reserved for - which, in a chunked server where
# num_of_partitions only ever grows, is every call that is itself a new high-water mark, since
# the branch above never lets the fresh computation run again once rt_params exists. On that
# call, exp_sums/max_logits/tmp_out stay sized for last call's (smaller) partition count while
# SDPA_STAGE_0 - whose own num_of_partitions comes from update_rt_params(), computed fresh every
# call and never stale - writes at strides keyed to the larger, current count.
#
# The change: compute the fresh (this-call) estimate unconditionally - the SAME two steps
# update_rt_params itself uses to turn max_context_len into rt_params->num_of_partitions, mirrored
# exactly rather than approximated: (1) the SWA block-skip shrink (desc->sliding_window > 0 &&
# stage == GENERATE && !has_scores_output()) that update_rt_params applies before dividing by
# partition_size - review finding 1: the first version of this patch skipped it, which made fresh
# strictly greater than stale on every decode step of any SWA model, not a rare high-water-mark
# case, silently breaking the "byte-identical on the common path" intent below; and (2) the
# PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS bound (patches/0015), now gated on rt_params->stage (the stage
# the STALE value was actually bounded under) whenever rt_params exists, rather than on
# fresh_stage - review finding 2: gating on fresh_stage let a PREFILL-stage call skip bounding
# for fresh while combining with a stale value from a different, non-PREFILL sequence the same
# impl handled earlier, so an unbounded fresh count could win the max() and lock in as the
# high-water mark past the configured bound. Then take num_of_partitions = max(fresh, rt_params's
# stale value) whenever rt_params exists, instead of trusting the stale value alone. Every call
# where fresh <= stale (the common case, since the buffer already grew past what this call needs)
# is byte-identical to before; only a call that is a new high-water mark changes, and only by
# sizing for what it is actually about to write. stage and partition_size selection are unchanged
# - still taken from rt_params when available, fresh otherwise - only num_of_partitions itself is
# touched. This also changes the rt_params-null path itself (the first call, or any call where
# rt_params was for some other reason zero): its else branch now takes fresh_num_of_partitions,
# which carries the SWA shrink the old branch never applied, so a sliding-window model's first
# GENERATE-stage call is sized SMALLER than before this patch - not a regression, since that
# smaller size is exactly what update_rt_params itself would compute for that same call; the old,
# unshrunk sizing on that path was the part that did not match production. Nothing else in
# get_internal_buffer_descs() changes.
#
# buf_elements_count, tmp_out_elements_count and the scores-output buffer (further down in this
# function, unchanged by this patch) are each monotone in num_of_partitions alone - a simple
# product with total_tokens/heads_num/v_head_size, none of which depend on whether stage and
# partition_size came from the same operand as num_of_partitions - so pairing a fresh
# num_of_partitions with a stale stage/partition_size can only over-allocate relative to what a
# fully-fresh recompute would have asked for, never under-allocate. get_max_context_len(), a
# mem_lock read of a device buffer, previously ran only on the first call (the pre-existing
# fallback branch) or when rt_params was otherwise unpopulated; it now runs unconditionally, every
# call, to produce the fresh estimate - a real per-call cost this patch adds, not hidden in the
# byte-identical claim above. get_max_context_len() itself does `memory_deps.at(MAX_CONTEXT_LEN)`,
# which throws rather than degrades if that dependency is absent - now reached on every call
# instead of only the pre-existing branch's calls.
#
# Noted for the record, not addressed by this patch: at PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS > 0, the
# fresh estimate clamps to that bound and stops growing once the raw partition count first
# exceeds it - so past that point this patch's max(fresh, stale) is constant, and cannot be the
# mechanism behind a bound-configuration failure that is still timing-sensitive past the point
# where the count has stopped changing. That failure stays open.
diff --git a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/sdpa/paged_attention_opt.cpp b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/sdpa/paged_attention_opt.cpp
index f0db814..8f1c6f0 100644
--- a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/sdpa/paged_attention_opt.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/sdpa/paged_attention_opt.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 // clang-format on
 #include "paged_attention_opt.hpp"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <memory>
@@ -1959,27 +1960,61 @@
         size_t partition_size = 256;
         size_t num_of_partitions = 1;
         auto* rt_params = static_cast<PagedAttentionRuntimeParams*>(m_rt_params.get());
+        // arcint (patches/0016): this function runs from realloc_intermediates(), BEFORE
+        // update_rt_params() computes THIS call's num_of_partitions - m_rt_params is a
+        // persistent member that update_rt_params() overwrites in place, so whenever it is
+        // non-null its num_of_partitions field still holds the PREVIOUS call's value at this
+        // point, not the one about to be dispatched. Always compute the fresh (this-call)
+        // estimate the same way update_rt_params computes rt_params->num_of_partitions itself
+        // (the SWA shrink below, and the PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS bound further down,
+        // patches/0015, both mirrored exactly - same condition, same value, not just the same
+        // shape), and never size smaller than either estimate.
+        const auto fresh_stage = get_paged_attention_stage(params);
+        const auto fresh_partition_size = get_partitioning_size(params, desc->v_head_size, fresh_stage);
+        const auto max_context_len = get_max_context_len(params);
+        // arcint (patches/0016, review finding 1): update_rt_params (~1668-1677) does not feed
+        // max_context_len straight into ceil_div - it first shrinks it to effective_context_len
+        // whenever desc->sliding_window > 0 && stage == GENERATE && !has_scores_output(), the
+        // SWA block-skip window. Skipping that shrink here made fresh strictly greater than
+        // stale on every decode step of any SWA model, not just on a high-water-mark call,
+        // silently defeating max(fresh, stale)'s intent to change nothing on the common path.
+        // Mirrored exactly, condition and arithmetic both, against fresh_stage (the stage this
+        // shrink would actually apply under for THIS call).
+        auto fresh_effective_context_len = max_context_len;
+        if (desc->sliding_window > 0 && fresh_stage == PagedAttentionStage::GENERATE && !desc->has_scores_output()) {
+            auto total_blocks = ceil_div(max_context_len, paged_attention_block_size);
+            auto swa_start_block = max_context_len > desc->sliding_window ? (max_context_len - desc->sliding_window) / paged_attention_block_size : 0;
+            auto effective_blocks = total_blocks - swa_start_block;
+            fresh_effective_context_len = effective_blocks * paged_attention_block_size;
+        }
+        size_t fresh_num_of_partitions = ceil_div(fresh_effective_context_len, fresh_partition_size);
+        // arcint (patches/0015, corrected by review finding 2): mirror update_rt_params'
+        // PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS bound here too, so a buffer-size query issued before
+        // rt_params exists reserves the same, bounded amount the bounded dispatch will actually
+        // address, rather than the raw (potentially much larger) partition count - see the
+        // matching comment in update_rt_params. Also excluded: has_scores_output() - see the
+        // matching comment there. Gated on rt_params->stage (the stage the STALE value was
+        // itself bounded under) whenever rt_params exists, not fresh_stage: gating on fresh_stage
+        // let a PREFILL-stage call skip bounding for fresh while combining with a stale value
+        // from a DIFFERENT, non-PREFILL sequence this same impl handled earlier - an unbounded
+        // fresh count could then win the max() and lock in as the high-water mark forever
+        // (realloc_intermediates() never shrinks). Using the stage that governs the value fresh
+        // is about to be compared against keeps both operands under one rule.
+        const auto bound_governing_stage = (rt_params != nullptr && rt_params->num_of_partitions != 0) ? rt_params->stage : fresh_stage;
+        if (bound_governing_stage != PagedAttentionStage::PREFILL && !desc->has_scores_output()) {
+            const auto max_partitions = params.get_program().get_config().get_paged_attention_max_partitions();
+            if (max_partitions > 0 && fresh_num_of_partitions > max_partitions) {
+                fresh_num_of_partitions = max_partitions;
+            }
+        }
         if (rt_params != nullptr && rt_params->num_of_partitions != 0) {
             stage = rt_params->stage;
             partition_size = rt_params->partition_size;
-            num_of_partitions = rt_params->num_of_partitions;
+            num_of_partitions = std::max(fresh_num_of_partitions, rt_params->num_of_partitions);
         } else {
-            stage = get_paged_attention_stage(params);
-            partition_size = get_partitioning_size(params, desc->v_head_size, stage);
-            const auto max_context_len = get_max_context_len(params);
-            num_of_partitions = ceil_div(max_context_len, partition_size);
-            // arcint (patches/0015): mirror update_rt_params' PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS
-            // bound here too, so a buffer-size query issued before rt_params exists (this
-            // branch) reserves the same, bounded amount that the bounded dispatch will actually
-            // address, rather than the raw (potentially much larger) partition count - see the
-            // matching comment in update_rt_params. Also excluded: has_scores_output() - see the
-            // matching comment there.
-            if (stage != PagedAttentionStage::PREFILL && !desc->has_scores_output()) {
-                const auto max_partitions = params.get_program().get_config().get_paged_attention_max_partitions();
-                if (max_partitions > 0 && num_of_partitions > max_partitions) {
-                    num_of_partitions = max_partitions;
-                }
-            }
+            stage = fresh_stage;
+            partition_size = fresh_partition_size;
+            num_of_partitions = fresh_num_of_partitions;
         }
         bool can_use_micro_sdpa = false;
 #ifdef ENABLE_ONEDNN_FOR_GPU
